# Scaffold markdown, and it must stay unformatted.
#
# The generators substitute __SCENE_DISPLAY_NAME__ / __GAME_DISPLAY_NAME__ into
# these files. Markdown reads __x__ as bold, so `prettier --write` rewrites the
# placeholder to **SCENE_DISPLAY_NAME** — the token no longer matches, the
# generator cannot replace it, and every scene generated afterwards ships a
# README with a literal placeholder in its first line.
#
# This is not hypothetical. It is the "broken display-name heading token" that
# tests/template/immersive-scene-template.naming.test.mjs asserts against, it
# had already happened once before that test was written, and running Prettier
# across the repo on 2026-08-01 reproduced it in all thirteen files.
src/templates/**/*.md
templates/**/*.md
